,["ARC or PLC in Clinton County","/arc-plc/pennsylvania/clinton-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids runs 75 years back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, August to September was 54% of normal and July to August was 65%. In 2026 so far, March to April came in at 146% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 25111 had its driest year in 1965 at 69% of normal.</p>"}
